<article class="env-definition" id="042L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/042L">Definition <span data-tag="042L">67.10.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. A morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$ is called a <em>monomorphism</em> if it is an injective map of sheaves, i.e., a monomorphism in the category of sheaves on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. </p>
